# The build context for deploy/Dockerfile is the repo root, so anything not
# excluded here is shipped to the Docker daemon on every build. Measured before
# this file existed: contracts/target alone is 3.3 GB, and the context was still
# climbing past 37 MB of virtualenvs and node_modules when it was interrupted.

.git/
.github/

# Virtualenvs and caches
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.pyc

# Node
**/node_modules/
dashboard/.next/

# Rust build output — by far the largest offender
contracts/target/
**/target/

# Secrets must never enter an image layer, not even a discarded build stage.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local state
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
.sterish-journal.json
deploy/artifacts/

# Not needed at runtime.
#
# docs/ is deliberately NOT excluded: sterish_pipeline.specs locates the repo by
# looking for docs/specs/verdict.schema.json and reads the frozen content_hash
# reference from docs/specs/reference/ at runtime. /use hashes the artifact
# through that module before serving it, so dropping docs/ would leave the paid
# path raising SpecsNotFound in production while every test still passed.
demo/
dashboard/
contracts/
**/tests/
